[2026-01-30T14:49:23.229Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ls2Ff39xXRhSBXy4UH8iHH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation: Unify animation utilities into shared library with hooks and theming\n     2→\n     3→## Context Area\n     4→Data Visualizations\n     5→\n     6→## Description\n     7→Unify animation utilities into shared library with hooks and theming\n     8→\n     9→## Implementation Details\n    10→\n    11→## Vision\n    12→Create a unified animation system that consolidates the scattered animation utilities, spring functions, and transition components across the video and visualization modules into a single, cohesive animation library with consistent easing, timing, and theming.\n    13→\n    14→## Business Value\n    15→- Eliminates code duplication across 15+ files that implement similar animation patterns\n    16→- Provides consistent animation behavior across all visualizations\n    17→- Reduces bundle size by consolidating duplicate spring/easing implementations\n    18→- Simplifies maintenance when animation behavior needs adjustment\n    19→\n    20→## Scope\n    21→**Included:**\n    22→- Consolidate spring, interpolate, easing functions from useVideoPlayback.ts\n    23→- Merge Transitions.tsx utilities (Crossfade, Slide, Scale, Stagger, etc.)\n    24→- Create unified animation hooks for common patterns\n    25→- Add theme-aware animation variants\n    26→\n    27→**Out of scope:**\n    28→- Rewriting visualization logic\n    29→- Changing Framer Motion dependency\n    30→\n    31→## Key Components\n    32→1. src/lib/animation/spring.ts - Consolidated spring physics\n    33→2. src/lib/animation/easing.ts - All easing curves in one place  \n    34→3. src/lib/animation/hooks.ts - useSpring, useStagger, useReveal hooks\n    35→4. src/lib/animation/transitions.tsx - Theme-aware transition components\n    36→\n    37→## Technical Approach\n    38→1. Extract all animation utilities from useVideoPlayback.ts into dedicated animation module\n    39→2. Refactor Transitions.tsx components to use the shared utilities\n    40→3. Create React hooks that wrap animation primitives with theme awareness\n    41→4. Update video components to import from new centralized location\n    42→5. Update visualization components to use consistent animation patterns\n    43→\n    44→## Files to Modify\n    45→- src/components/report/video/useVideoPlayback.ts - Extract animation functions\n    46→- src/components/report/video/Transitions.tsx - Refactor to use shared utilities\n    47→- src/components/report/video/AnimatedCharts.tsx - Use shared spring\n    48→- src/components/report/visualizations/Timeline.tsx - Use shared transitions\n    49→- src/components/report/visualizations/NetworkGraph.tsx - Use shared animation hooks\n    50→- Create new src/lib/animation/ directory with consolidated modules\n    51→\n    52→## Success Criteria\n    53→- [ ] All animation utilities live in one place\n    54→- [ ] Zero duplicate spring/easing implementations across codebase\n    55→- [ ] All visualization components use shared animation hooks\n    56→- [ ] Animation timing is consistent across all visualizations\n    57→\n    58→## Potential Challenges\n    59→- Framer Motion and custom spring implementations may have subtle differences - test thoroughly\n    60→- Some components may have bespoke timing requirements - provide escape hatches\n    61→\n    62→## Instructions\n    63→\n    64→1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n    65→2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n    66→3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n    67→4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n    68→5. Test the changes work as expected\n    69→\n    70→## Notes\n    71→\n    72→This requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\n    73→Focus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n    74→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a","uuid":"0156f67b-da0b-4288-ad76-8f7be9af4d3e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\dir-1769783005762-unify-animation-utilities-into-shared.md","content":"# Implementation: Unify animation utilities into shared library with hooks and theming\n\n## Context Area\nData Visualizations\n\n## Description\nUnify animation utilities into shared library with hooks and theming\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\nCreate a unified animation system that consolidates the scattered animation utilities, spring functions, and transition components across the video and visualization modules into a single, cohesive animation library with consistent easing, timing, and theming.\n\n## Business Value\n- Eliminates code duplication across 15+ files that implement similar animation patterns\n- Provides consistent animation behavior across all visualizations\n- Reduces bundle size by consolidating duplicate spring/easing implementations\n- Simplifies maintenance when animation behavior needs adjustment\n\n## Scope\n**Included:**\n- Consolidate spring, interpolate, easing functions from useVideoPlayback.ts\n- Merge Transitions.tsx utilities (Crossfade, Slide, Scale, Stagger, etc.)\n- Create unified animation hooks for common patterns\n- Add theme-aware animation variants\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- Rewriting visualization logic\n- Changing Framer Motion dependency\n\n## Key Components\n1. src/lib/animation/spring.ts - Consolidated spring physics\n2. src/lib/animation/easing.ts - All easing curves in one place  \n3. src/lib/animation/hooks.ts - useSpring, useStagger, useReveal hooks\n4. src/lib/animation/transitions.tsx - Theme-aware transition components\n\n## Technical Approach\n1. Extract all animation utilities from useVideoPlayback.ts into dedicated animation module\n2. Refactor Transitions.tsx components to use the shared utilities\n3. Create React hooks that wrap animation primitives with theme awareness\n4. Update video components to import from new centralized location\n5. Update visualization components to use consistent animation patterns\n\n## Files to Modify\n- src/components/report/video/useVideoPlayback.ts - Extract animation functions\n- src/components/report/video/Transitions.tsx - Refactor to use shared utilities\n- src/components/report/video/AnimatedCharts.tsx - Use shared spring\n- src/components/report/visualizations/Timeline.tsx - Use shared transitions\n- src/components/report/visualizations/NetworkGraph.tsx - Use shared animation hooks\n- Create new src/lib/animation/ directory with consolidated modules\n\n## Success Criteria\n- [ ] All animation utilities live in one place\n- [ ] Zero duplicate spring/easing implementations across codebase\n- [ ] All visualization components use shared animation hooks\n- [ ] Animation timing is consistent across all visualizations\n\n## Potential Challenges\n- Framer Motion and custom spring implementations may have subtle differences - test thoroughly\n- Some components may have bespoke timing requirements - provide escape hatches\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
